00:11:47,143 --> 00:11:48,778
It's one thing to get
pulled into danger.

253
00:11:48,813 --> 00:11:50,380
It's another to
go looking for it.

254
00:11:50,413 --> 00:11:52,525
You're a wanted fugitive,
Turner. It's too big of a risk.

255
00:11:52,549 --> 00:11:54,684
Is this about me getting
caught or me getting hurt?

256
00:11:57,087 --> 00:11:58,688
It's about your
dad not wanting you

257
00:11:58,722 --> 00:12:00,490
to follow down the same path.

258
00:12:06,029 --> 00:12:08,265
You can't just walk into
the GCPD and take evidence.

259
00:12:08,298 --> 00:12:10,567
You can if you're in a
cop uniform holding these.

260
00:12:11,635 --> 00:12:13,703
Evidence transfer requests.
Some of my best work.

261
00:12:15,705 --> 00:12:17,808
Just a couple of hours in
the Gotham Academy Art Lab.

262
00:12:17,842 --> 00:12:19,810
Duela: Let me see.

263
00:12:19,844 --> 00:12:22,078
Oh. Looks like the
real deal to me.

264
00:12:22,112 --> 00:12:23,957
Harper: Your mug shot is
plastered all over the city.

265
00:12:23,981 --> 00:12:25,615
How are you not
gonna be recognized?

266
00:12:25,649 --> 00:12:27,350
I could help with that.

267
00:12:27,384 --> 00:12:28,953
Look, they only know
me as a scared kid.

268
00:12:28,986 --> 00:12:30,129
They're not expecting
a rookie cop.

269
00:12:30,153 --> 00:12:32,088
Yeah. Exactly.
Which you aren't.

270
00:12:32,122 --> 00:12:33,723
This is too dangerous.

271
00:12:33,757 --> 00:12:35,358
Yeah. Yeah, it is.

272
00:12:35,392 --> 00:12:39,129
And you know what?
He can handle it.

273
00:12:39,162 --> 00:12:41,008
The Talon would have
turned me into a patty melt

274
00:12:41,032 --> 00:12:42,441
if he hadn't pulled
me out of that car.

275
00:12:42,465 --> 00:12:44,100
And, aah, your problem
is that you are

276
00:12:44,134 --> 00:12:45,970
so busy trying to
protect your brother

277
00:12:46,003 --> 00:12:48,039
that you haven't noticed
that he doesn't need it.

278
00:12:48,071 --> 00:12:49,907
So, maybe it's time
for you to recognize

279
00:12:49,941 --> 00:12:51,374
that he's a total badass.

280
00:12:56,079 --> 00:12:58,148
Toodles.

281
00:12:58,181 --> 00:13:00,650
Thanks for sticking up for me.

282
00:13:00,684 --> 00:13:01,895
It's nice to have
someone believe in me

283
00:13:01,919 --> 00:13:03,854
even if it is you.

284
00:13:03,888 --> 00:13:06,456
Oh, yeah, I just
said that because

285
00:13:06,489 --> 00:13:09,526
there's something I
need you to do for me.

286
00:13:12,495 --> 00:13:16,132
KiNG MALA: ♪ I don't
need your roses, I like ♪

287
00:13:16,166 --> 00:13:19,603
♪ Men on their knees ♪

288
00:13:19,636 --> 00:13:26,476
♪ Praying up to their god,
seein' visions of me ♪

289
00:13:26,509 --> 00:13:31,147
♪ I'm a cult leader, mind
reader, heart eater ♪

290
00:13:31,181 --> 00:13:34,852
♪ Fear feeder, say I'm
your favorite preacher ♪

291
00:13:34,885 --> 00:13:39,689
♪ If I wasn't a narcissist,
I wouldn't like me either ♪

292
00:13:39,723 --> 00:13:41,300
Woman: Mr. March, can we
get a picture over here?

293
00:13:41,324 --> 00:13:43,226
KiNG MALA: ♪ I'm
a cult leader... ♪

294
00:13:43,259 --> 00:13:44,661
Mr. and Mrs. March.

295
00:13:44,694 --> 00:13:46,162
Please, call me Rebecca.

296
00:13:46,196 --> 00:13:47,530
It's nice to finally meet you.

297
00:13:48,765 --> 00:13:51,035
Rebecca: It's a shame we
won't be seeing your parents.

298
00:13:51,068 --> 00:13:54,105
Your mom's been MIA from
the club for weeks now.

299
00:13:54,137 --> 00:13:56,306
Yeah, Dad's taping
"Quiz Bowl" tonight.

300
00:13:56,339 --> 00:13:58,843
Mom's been spending more time
at the studio to support him.

301
00:13:58,876 --> 00:14:01,478
Rebecca: Of course. Well,
they must be so proud.

302
00:14:01,511 --> 00:14:04,180
Brody told us you're on
the fast track for MIT,

303
00:14:04,214 --> 00:14:06,050
following in your
dad's footsteps.

304
00:14:06,083 --> 00:14:08,251
Same as Brody now
going to State.

305
00:14:08,284 --> 00:14:11,187
Heard you were quite the
fencer in your day, Mr. March.

306
00:14:11,221 --> 00:14:12,857
Won State 4 years running.

307
00:14:12,890 --> 00:14:14,157
Shall we?

308
00:14:16,693 --> 00:14:17,962
No pressure.

309
00:14:17,995 --> 00:14:19,596
Lincoln: You'll do
fine. I'm certain.

310
00:14:19,629 --> 00:14:21,798
Though I doubt we can
count on your next opponent

311
00:14:21,832 --> 00:14:24,935
also being arrested for
murdering his own father.

312
00:14:24,969 --> 00:14:26,369
Hey. How you doing?

313
00:14:26,403 --> 00:14:28,939
KiNG MALA: ♪
Leader, leader, no ♪

314
00:14:28,973 --> 00:14:32,776
♪ Leader, leader, leader, no ♪

315
00:14:34,145 --> 00:14:36,379
[Tool whirring, snapping]

316
00:14:47,724 --> 00:14:48,725
[Chirp]

317
00:14:58,668 --> 00:14:59,837
[Gun clicks]

318
00:14:59,870 --> 00:15:02,605
[Laughs]

319
00:15:06,276 --> 00:15:08,278
Hi there.

320
00:15:08,311 --> 00:15:10,280
[Whack] [Thud]

321
00:15:11,214 --> 00:15:13,050
[Whispering] Turner,
what are you doing here?

322
00:15:13,084 --> 00:15:15,986
Waiting on a "thank you" for
stopping him from shooting you?

323
00:15:16,020 --> 00:15:18,288
One, I had him.
Two, now I can't

324
00:15:18,321 --> 00:15:21,158
question him to find out
what they were planning next.

325
00:15:21,192 --> 00:15:22,425
So, thank you.

326
00:15:23,493 --> 00:15:25,129
How'd you even find this place?

327
00:15:25,162 --> 00:15:26,931
The rocket that took
down that airship

328
00:15:26,964 --> 00:15:29,566
came from the north, so,
from the point of impact,

329
00:15:29,599 --> 00:15:31,301
it's a straight
line to this area.

330
00:15:31,334 --> 00:15:34,071
There are, like, 50
warehouses in this area.

331
00:15:34,105 --> 00:15:35,772
How did you narrow
it down to this one?

332
00:15:36,841 --> 00:15:39,542
When I was little, my dad
and I used to play a game.

333
00:15:39,576 --> 00:15:41,411
He called it "Sore Thumb."

334
00:15:41,444 --> 00:15:43,814
Wherever we were...
Dinners, parties...

335
00:15:43,848 --> 00:15:45,082
He would have me pick out

336
00:15:45,116 --> 00:15:46,716
the thing that didn't belong.

337
00:15:46,750 --> 00:15:48,152
I always thought
it was just a game

338
00:15:48,185 --> 00:15:49,385
to entertain a bored kid,

339
00:15:49,419 --> 00:15:50,821
but turns out...

340
00:15:50,855 --> 00:15:52,823
He was teaching you
situational awareness.

341
00:15:52,857 --> 00:15:55,592
Yup. So, when I saw
that this warehouse

342
00:15:55,625 --> 00:15:57,694
was the only one
without security lights

343
00:15:57,727 --> 00:16:00,296
and the gates were
padlocked from the inside,

344
00:16:00,330 --> 00:16:02,833
I suspected somebody was
trying to hide something.

345
00:16:04,734 --> 00:16:07,872
Looks like you put those
skills to good use.

346
00:16:07,905 --> 00:16:09,950
I just can't figure out why
he would teach them to me

347
00:16:09,974 --> 00:16:11,307
if he didn't want
me to use them.

348
00:16:12,243 --> 00:16:13,576
I'm sure he had a reason.

349
00:16:23,686 --> 00:16:25,956
Turner: These are
from Ace Chemicals.

350
00:16:25,990 --> 00:16:27,925
So, it wasn't a
terrorist attack.

351
00:16:27,958 --> 00:16:29,769
Crashing that airship into Ace
Chemicals was to cover the fact

352
00:16:29,793 --> 00:16:31,528
that the Mutants were
robbing the place.

353
00:16:31,561 --> 00:16:33,721
What are they planning to do
with a bunch of chemicals?

354
00:16:40,271 --> 00:16:41,504
They're empty.

355
00:16:43,773 --> 00:16:45,775
Whatever they were planning,
they already did it.

356
00:16:52,917 --> 00:16:55,186
[Classical music playing]
[Indistinct chatter]

357
00:16:59,792 --> 00:17:01,192
Good to see you, Martin.

358
00:17:05,731 --> 00:17:06,931
Miss Brown.

359
00:17:08,734 --> 00:17:09,768
How are you this evening?

360
00:17:09,802 --> 00:17:10,968
Ah. Should I get my lawyer

361
00:17:11,002 --> 00:17:12,404
down here before I answer that?

362
00:17:13,539 --> 00:17:15,306
Lincoln: Harvey Dent.

363
00:17:15,339 --> 00:17:19,143
Gotham's white
knight... in black tie.

364
00:17:19,177 --> 00:17:21,245
Lincoln. Good to see you.

365
00:17:21,279 --> 00:17:23,649
Have you met my wife Rebecca?

366
00:17:23,682 --> 00:17:26,585
No, I don't believe I
have. Pleasure to meet you.

367
00:17:26,618 --> 00:17:29,521
So, if you're here
glad-handing the donor class,

368
00:17:29,555 --> 00:17:31,289
I assume the rumors are true

369
00:17:31,322 --> 00:17:32,791
and you are running for mayor.

370
00:17:32,825 --> 00:17:34,058
Right now, my focus is on

371
00:17:34,091 --> 00:17:36,160
the current job I
was elected to do.

372
00:17:36,194 --> 00:17:37,796
Is that right? All right.

373
00:17:37,830 --> 00:17:39,631
Well, if you ever hope to be

374
00:17:39,665 --> 00:17:41,533
a politician in this town,

375
00:17:41,567 --> 00:17:43,535
better learn how to
lie better than that.

376
00:17:47,806 --> 00:17:49,149
I have to disagree
with my husband.

377
00:17:49,173 --> 00:17:51,042
I think you lie quite well.

378
00:17:53,779 --> 00:17:56,515
I almost believed you when
you told him we'd never met.

379
00:18:01,085 --> 00:18:03,287
[Helicopter flying]

380
00:18:03,321 --> 00:18:05,557
[Elevator bell dings]
[Indistinct chatter]

381
00:18:09,495 --> 00:18:12,163
Desk sergeant: Sign 'em out,
you gotta sign 'em back in.

382
00:18:12,196 --> 00:18:14,666
It's called chain of custody.

383
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:15,734
Yeah.

384
00:18:17,268 --> 00:18:18,302
Ahem.

385
00:18:20,004 --> 00:18:21,272
How you doing?

386
00:18:22,774 --> 00:18:24,919
Desk sergeant: What do you want? Cullen:
Yeah, I'm from Somerset Precinct.

387
00:18:24,943 --> 00:18:26,454
I just got a case
file transfer request.

388
00:18:26,478 --> 00:18:28,580
Does this look like the
Records Room to you?

389
00:18:28,614 --> 00:18:30,047
Uh, uh...

390
00:18:30,081 --> 00:18:31,358
Down the hall, third
door on the left.

391
00:18:31,382 --> 00:18:33,685
Look for a sign
that says "Records."

392
00:18:36,955 --> 00:18:38,155
Hey.

393
00:18:41,693 --> 00:18:43,103
Do they not teach you
anything over there

394
00:18:43,127 --> 00:18:44,563
at Somerset, rook?

395
00:18:46,498 --> 00:18:50,502
Coffee. You come into another
man's shop asking for stuff,

396
00:18:50,536 --> 00:18:52,471
a little juice of the
bean goes a long way.

397
00:18:52,504 --> 00:18:54,540
Right. I'll... I'll remember
that, sir. Thank you.

398
00:18:54,573 --> 00:18:56,775
Yeah. I'll remember you.

399
00:18:58,644 --> 00:19:00,712
[Speaking Spanish]

400
00:19:02,113 --> 00:19:03,381
[Door closes]

401
00:19:05,984 --> 00:19:08,286
Uh, what's all this?

402
00:19:08,319 --> 00:19:10,154
We were kind of hoping
you could tell us.

403
00:19:10,187 --> 00:19:12,032
We found these chemicals
and some kind of blueprints

404
00:19:12,056 --> 00:19:14,158
trashed at a Mutant
Gang stash house.

405
00:19:14,191 --> 00:19:16,260
Any idea what they're up to?

406
00:19:16,294 --> 00:19:18,630
Well, you've got nitrobromide

407
00:19:18,664 --> 00:19:20,097
and uridium oxidate.

408
00:19:20,131 --> 00:19:21,767
Not much you can
make out of those.

409
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:24,536
They're both solubles. They
wouldn't even cause a reaction

410
00:19:24,570 --> 00:19:28,607
unless they were put under
pressure and aerosolized.

411
00:19:31,910 --> 00:19:33,712
Damn. It looks
like they're making

412
00:19:33,745 --> 00:19:35,480
some kind of poison gas bomb.

413
00:19:35,514 --> 00:19:36,715
To gas the city?

414
00:19:36,748 --> 00:19:38,115
No. If you release
it outdoors,

415
00:19:38,149 --> 00:19:39,518
it'll dissipate too quickly.

416
00:19:39,551 --> 00:19:41,161
For it to work, it needs
to stay concentrated,

417
00:19:41,185 --> 00:19:42,721
like in an enclosed area.

418
00:19:42,754 --> 00:19:44,388
Turner: The GCPD. Carrie: No.

419
00:19:44,423 --> 00:19:46,992
Now that the cops
have Vernon in a cage,

420
00:19:47,025 --> 00:19:48,201
I don't think the
Mutant Gang would risk

421
00:19:48,225 --> 00:19:49,595
killing their leader.

422
00:19:49,628 --> 00:19:51,362
Duela: I know what
my daddy would do.

423
00:19:55,299 --> 00:19:56,635
He would make a statement.

424
00:19:59,504 --> 00:20:03,207
All right. What
does poison gas do?

425
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:04,743
Uh, it kills people?

426
00:20:04,776 --> 00:20:06,445
Well, yes, but how?

427
00:20:06,478 --> 00:20:08,221
Carrie: It chokes you to
death. Duela: Ding ding ding!

428
00:20:08,245 --> 00:20:10,449
Yes. And who better
to choke with it

429
00:20:10,482 --> 00:20:12,751
than the people who've
had Gotham by the throat

430
00:20:12,784 --> 00:20:14,052
since the very beginning?

431
00:20:14,086 --> 00:20:16,153
The ones who are, as we speak,

432
00:20:16,187 --> 00:20:18,824
congratulating themselves
between bites of

433
00:20:18,857 --> 00:20:20,291
little, overpriced fish eggs.

434
00:20:20,324 --> 00:20:21,292
The Founders Gala.

435
00:20:21,325 --> 00:20:22,293
Yes! You are on fire

436
00:20:22,326 --> 00:20:23,662
today, Little Bird.

437
00:20:23,695 --> 00:20:24,763
I mean, come on. All those

438
00:20:24,796 --> 00:20:25,897
well-heeled hypocrites,

439
00:20:25,931 --> 00:20:28,332
just gasping for rarefied air.

440
00:20:28,366 --> 00:20:30,636
The mayor. The
district attorney.

441
00:20:30,669 --> 00:20:31,703
Stephanie.

442
00:20:32,738 --> 00:20:35,139
[Classical music playing]
[Indistinct chatter]

443
00:20:38,242 --> 00:20:39,811
Two virgin mojitos.

444
00:20:43,415 --> 00:20:45,851
Really? 'Cause this one
tastes pretty slutty to me.

445
00:20:45,884 --> 00:20:48,620
Yeah, I tipped the bartender
a 20 to pretend I'm 21.

446
00:20:48,654 --> 00:20:50,364
You know, given our recent
brushes with the law,

447
00:20:50,388 --> 00:20:51,923
I'm not sure adding
underage drinking

448
00:20:51,957 --> 00:20:53,458
to our rap sheets
is a good idea.

449
00:20:53,492 --> 00:20:55,259
You're about to have
dinner with my parents.

450
00:20:55,292 --> 00:20:57,562
Trust me, you are
going to need it.

451
00:20:57,596 --> 00:20:58,630
[Glasses clink]

452
00:21:01,600 --> 00:21:02,567
Your mom seems nice.

453
00:21:02,601 --> 00:21:04,201
[Chuckles]

454
00:21:04,235 --> 00:21:05,570
And my dad?

455
00:21:07,639 --> 00:21:08,807
Your mom seems nice.

456
00:21:08,840 --> 00:21:11,843
Huh. Yeah. She is.

457
00:21:15,647 --> 00:21:18,349
It's not always easy being
married to Lincoln March,

458
00:21:18,382 --> 00:21:20,619
even though she makes
it seem that way.

459
00:21:20,652 --> 00:21:23,187
Starting to get the sense
it's not easy being his son.

460
00:21:26,792 --> 00:21:30,495
[Cell phone buzzing]

461
00:21:30,529 --> 00:21:32,431
I have to get this. Sorry.

462
00:21:32,464 --> 00:21:33,465
Yeah.

463
00:21:35,834 --> 00:21:39,037
Yes, the party is awful,
the lava cake is garbage,

464
00:21:39,071 --> 00:21:40,782
my feet are killing me, and
I'm having a terrible time.

465
00:21:40,806 --> 00:21:43,108
Turner: Steph, listen. You
have to get out of there.

466
00:21:43,141 --> 00:21:44,275
What? Why?

467
00:21:44,308 --> 00:21:45,644
The Mutant Gang's about to do

468
00:21:45,677 --> 00:21:46,878
something terrible.

469
00:21:46,912 --> 00:21:48,447
[Indistinct voice
on police radio]

470
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:50,247
[Gunfire]

471
00:21:50,281 --> 00:21:51,993
Officer: Who was that?
Officer 2: Shots fired.

472
00:21:52,017 --> 00:21:53,284
[Gunfire, glass breaking]

473
00:21:53,317 --> 00:21:55,053
[Indistinct voice
on police radio]

474
00:21:55,087 --> 00:21:57,122
Man: Grenade!

475
00:21:57,155 --> 00:21:59,658
[People screaming]

476
00:21:59,691 --> 00:22:01,760
[Crowd screaming]

477
00:22:14,673 --> 00:22:16,842
No need to panic.

478
00:22:16,875 --> 00:22:20,244
We're just here to provide
the evening's entertainment.

479
00:22:21,213 --> 00:22:23,148
Do you all like games?

480
00:22:23,181 --> 00:22:26,685
Because I have one that
I think you'll love.

481
00:22:28,787 --> 00:22:30,655
It's a very simple game.

482
00:22:30,689 --> 00:22:31,923
It's called...

483
00:22:33,324 --> 00:22:35,259
"What Does This Button Do?"

484
00:22:37,596 --> 00:22:40,232
Male reporter: It's a chaotic
scene here at City Hall

485
00:22:40,264 --> 00:22:42,768
as the Founders Gala
has been taken hostage

486
00:22:42,801 --> 00:22:45,570
by the Mutant Gang, who have
barricaded themselves inside,

487
00:22:45,604 --> 00:22:49,174
threatening to detonate
a chemical explosive

488
00:22:49,207 --> 00:22:51,443
if the GCPD does not
release their leader,

489
00:22:51,476 --> 00:22:54,179
Vernon Wagner, by
10 p.m. tonight.

490
00:22:54,212 --> 00:22:57,314
In these dark times,
I'm sure I'm not alone

491
00:22:57,348 --> 00:23:00,786
in feeling that Gotham
could use a Batman.

492
00:23:00,819 --> 00:23:04,456
Woman on TV: Isn't that the
truth? In other news, Gotham...

493
00:23:07,461 --> 00:23:09,563
So, you guys are... going in?

494
00:23:09,595 --> 00:23:10,940
We were kind of hoping
you would join us.

495
00:23:10,964 --> 00:23:12,432
Uh, why the hell
would I do that?

496
00:23:12,466 --> 00:23:13,706
You know how to disable a bomb.

497
00:23:13,733 --> 00:23:15,769
Yeah. Step One:
call the bomb squad.

498
00:23:15,802 --> 00:23:18,939
Carrie: They don't have the
instruction manual. We do.

499
00:23:18,972 --> 00:23:20,841
Besides, if they go in
and kick the door down,

500
00:23:20,874 --> 00:23:22,552
then the Mutants will
just set off the bomb.

501
00:23:22,576 --> 00:23:24,711
Sorry, how is what you're
planning any different?

502
00:23:24,744 --> 00:23:27,314
Well, you don't have to
go through the front door.

503
00:23:27,347 --> 00:23:30,383
Decommissioned subway tunnels
will take you right under it.

504
00:23:30,417 --> 00:23:32,052
Then you could pop
up into City Hall

505
00:23:32,085 --> 00:23:34,121
like a stripper
popping out of a cake.

506
00:23:34,154 --> 00:23:36,655
But you would need someone to
open the door from the inside.

507
00:23:36,689 --> 00:23:39,192
If I could arrange that,
would you show us the way?

508
00:23:39,226 --> 00:23:41,528
Why would I risk my life
to save a bunch of people

509
00:23:41,561 --> 00:23:42,829
who don't give a damn about me?

510
00:23:42,863 --> 00:23:44,464
Same reason we saved
you from the Talon.

511
00:23:44,498 --> 00:23:45,698
You do realize it's impossible

512
00:23:45,732 --> 00:23:47,234
to guilt me into
anything, right?

513
00:23:48,735 --> 00:23:50,937
Fine. You'll get to
punch a bunch of Mutants.

514
00:23:50,971 --> 00:23:53,406
Oh! Should've led with that.

515
00:23:53,440 --> 00:23:54,774
I'll get my purse.

516
00:23:57,244 --> 00:24:00,080
P.A.: All officers, report
to the briefing room.

517
00:24:03,583 --> 00:24:05,452
You.

518
00:24:05,485 --> 00:24:07,120
Briefing. Now.

519
00:24:07,154 --> 00:24:09,232
I really gotta get these records
down to Somerset, though.

520
00:24:09,256 --> 00:24:10,490
All hands on deck, rook.

521
00:24:10,524 --> 00:24:12,691
Hostage situation at City Hall.

522
00:24:12,726 --> 00:24:14,261
Man: Briefing room. Now.

523
00:24:22,369 --> 00:24:24,504
Man: Take a seat.

524
00:24:24,538 --> 00:24:26,573
All right now. All
right, everybody.

525
00:24:26,606 --> 00:24:28,441
Listen up. Settle down.

526
00:24:28,475 --> 00:24:29,843
We got a hostage situation.

527
00:24:29,876 --> 00:24:32,112
[Helicopter flying]

528
00:24:37,384 --> 00:24:40,086
[Bell rings] [Banging]

529
00:24:46,092 --> 00:24:47,294
[Banging]

530
00:24:51,164 --> 00:24:53,176
Here you thought you wouldn't
make this year's Gala.

531
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:55,535
Not exactly how I wanted
to join the party.

532
00:24:55,569 --> 00:24:56,870
Carrie: Everyone, stay on comms.

533
00:24:56,903 --> 00:24:58,205
I'll do a sweep while you guys

534
00:24:58,238 --> 00:24:59,906
figure out where
they put the bomb.

535
00:24:59,940 --> 00:25:01,217
For maximum dispersal,
they'll have put it

536
00:25:01,241 --> 00:25:02,275
in the HVAC system.

537
00:25:02,309 --> 00:25:03,743
Boiler room's this way.

538
00:25:03,777 --> 00:25:04,820
But there might be
some of those Mutants

539
00:25:04,844 --> 00:25:06,112
between here and there.

540
00:25:12,519 --> 00:25:13,753
Duela: Yah! Mutant: Uhh!

541
00:25:15,655 --> 00:25:18,191
Duela: Hmm. [Pipe clatters]

542
00:25:19,793 --> 00:25:21,528
We gotta get this
thing out of here.

543
00:25:21,561 --> 00:25:23,396
Harper: Wait, wait.

544
00:25:23,430 --> 00:25:24,664
See that?

545
00:25:24,698 --> 00:25:26,433
It's a mercury tilt switch.

546
00:25:26,466 --> 00:25:28,068
Used to use it in
old thermostats.

547
00:25:28,101 --> 00:25:29,903
You move it, mercury
closes the circuit.

548
00:25:29,936 --> 00:25:31,371
Uh, what does that mean?

549
00:25:31,404 --> 00:25:32,515
Harper: It means the Mutants

550
00:25:32,539 --> 00:25:33,583
are smarter than we thought.

551
00:25:33,607 --> 00:25:36,643
You move this thing... boom.

552
00:25:36,676 --> 00:25:38,211
Then we have to disable it here.

553
00:25:44,217 --> 00:25:47,254
Mutant: All right, listen
up. Rings, watches.

554
00:25:47,287 --> 00:25:50,190
Trinkets. All in the bag.

555
00:25:50,223 --> 00:25:53,193
Make a donation,
everybody. Let's go.

556
00:25:53,226 --> 00:25:54,828
Mutant 2: I'll take
that. Rebecca: Brody.

557
00:25:54,861 --> 00:25:56,896
Brody: Uhh! Mutant
1: Come on, come on.

558
00:26:03,570 --> 00:26:06,215
Woman on phone: There's a lot of red tape
and I don't have that kind of authority.

559
00:26:06,239 --> 00:26:08,284
I don't care how much red
tape you've gotta cut through.

560
00:26:08,308 --> 00:26:10,143
There's gonna be a
lot more red down here

561
00:26:10,176 --> 00:26:11,011
if you don't!

562
00:26:11,044 --> 00:26:13,714
Release him. On my order.

563
00:26:13,748 --> 00:26:16,717
Huh. You hear that?

564
00:26:16,751 --> 00:26:18,251
So, here's what you're gonna do.

565
00:26:22,989 --> 00:26:25,091
Do I honestly have to
tell you what will happen

566
00:26:25,125 --> 00:26:27,027
if you give in to their demands?

567
00:26:27,060 --> 00:26:29,229
Um, we make it
out of this alive?

568
00:26:29,262 --> 00:26:32,832
You will be sending a
message to every criminal

569
00:26:32,866 --> 00:26:35,235
that not only do we
negotiate with terrorists,

570
00:26:35,268 --> 00:26:36,903
but we give them
everything they want.

571
00:26:36,936 --> 00:26:38,872
Hardly. We're trading
one Mutant Leader

572
00:26:38,905 --> 00:26:40,440
for the rest of his gang.

573
00:26:40,473 --> 00:26:41,742
This place is surrounded.

574
00:26:41,776 --> 00:26:43,410
They're not getting outta here.

575
00:26:43,443 --> 00:26:46,613
And I am sending a message
to the criminals, Harvey.

576
00:26:46,646 --> 00:26:48,214
Don't mess with us.

577
00:26:56,156 --> 00:26:57,891
Careful. Don't
want to get bomb

578
00:26:57,924 --> 00:26:59,359
all over your Valentino.

579
00:26:59,392 --> 00:27:00,593
It's a May Nickel.

580
00:27:00,627 --> 00:27:02,862
And that is a mutating algorithm

581
00:27:02,896 --> 00:27:04,864
that deletes itself
once complete.

582
00:27:04,898 --> 00:27:07,600
Turner: Uh, what happens
when it deletes itself?

583
00:27:07,634 --> 00:27:08,736
It deletes us.

584
00:27:08,769 --> 00:27:11,271
[Tape ripping]

585
00:27:11,304 --> 00:27:12,639
Don't want this
one getting loose

586
00:27:12,672 --> 00:27:14,274
while I go handle his buddies.

587
00:27:14,307 --> 00:27:17,143
Harper: Uh, guys? I just
searched for the frequency

588
00:27:17,177 --> 00:27:18,511
that'll deactivate this thing

589
00:27:18,545 --> 00:27:20,647
and there isn't one.

590
00:27:20,680 --> 00:27:22,282
Just one to activate it.

591
00:27:22,315 --> 00:27:24,060
So, it was meant to turn
on and never turn off.

592
00:27:24,084 --> 00:27:26,019
So, the bomb's going
off no matter what?

593
00:27:26,052 --> 00:27:28,021
That'd kill the
Mutants along with us.

594
00:27:29,189 --> 00:27:30,857
Unless they planned ahead.

595
00:27:31,958 --> 00:27:33,393
They all brought these.

596
00:27:34,361 --> 00:27:36,162
Maybe they always
intended to gas the place.

597
00:27:36,196 --> 00:27:38,698
Duela: Gotta say, it's kind
of the perfect escape plan.

598
00:27:38,733 --> 00:27:41,568
The GCPD releases the Mutant
Leader, they set off the bomb.

599
00:27:41,601 --> 00:27:44,938
The GCPD doesn't release the Mutant
Leader, they set off the bomb,

600
00:27:44,971 --> 00:27:46,315
and then they all
peace out of here while

601
00:27:46,339 --> 00:27:48,375
seizures and
suffocation get to fight

602
00:27:48,408 --> 00:27:49,844
over what kills us first.

603
00:27:49,876 --> 00:27:51,712
Great. Huh. Just
gonna hang on to this.

604
00:27:51,746 --> 00:27:53,222
How much time do we
have to defuse it?

605
00:27:53,246 --> 00:27:54,514
42 minutes. And that's if

606
00:27:54,547 --> 00:27:55,648
the GCPD doesn't release

607
00:27:55,682 --> 00:27:56,727
the Mutant Leader before then.

608
00:27:56,751 --> 00:27:58,051
We have to warn them not to.

609
00:27:58,084 --> 00:27:59,462
Buy ourselves as much
time as possible.

610
00:27:59,486 --> 00:28:01,126
Yeah. We're the last
ones they'll believe.

611
00:28:02,055 --> 00:28:06,292
There is one person the
GCPD will believe. Harvey.

612
00:28:07,728 --> 00:28:10,063
I just gotta make
him believe me first.

613
00:28:10,096 --> 00:28:12,332
OK, and if he doesn't,
he'll have you arrested.

614
00:28:14,567 --> 00:28:15,902
You're gonna risk that?

615
00:28:17,838 --> 00:28:19,572
A lot of people
will die if I don't.

616
00:28:22,011 --> 00:28:23,278
Mutant: Sit down now. Quiet.

617
00:28:23,311 --> 00:28:25,380
Nobody's gonna get hurt.

618
00:28:25,413 --> 00:28:26,815
Mutant 2: Calm down.

619
00:28:26,848 --> 00:28:29,185
We've already taken
what we wanted from you.

620
00:28:29,217 --> 00:28:30,485
Have a seat.

621
00:28:32,220 --> 00:28:33,555
Come with me.

622
00:28:33,588 --> 00:28:35,356
Mutant: Sit down now. Quiet.

623
00:28:36,558 --> 00:28:39,627
Ahh. OK. OK.

624
00:28:40,762 --> 00:28:43,065
If you're gonna kill me,
just get it over with.

625
00:28:43,099 --> 00:28:44,499
I'm not gonna kill you.

626
00:28:46,568 --> 00:28:47,635
Turner.

627
00:28:50,572 --> 00:28:52,774
What the hell are
you doing here?

628
00:28:52,807 --> 00:28:53,975
We don't have much time.

629
00:28:55,477 --> 00:28:57,278
That gas bomb is
in the boiler room,

630
00:28:57,312 --> 00:28:58,789
and as soon as their leader
is released, the Mutant Gang

631
00:28:58,813 --> 00:28:59,881
are gonna set it off.

632
00:28:59,914 --> 00:29:01,316
That's their exit strategy.

633
00:29:01,349 --> 00:29:03,018
Kill everybody here,

634
00:29:03,052 --> 00:29:04,153
escape in the chaos.

635
00:29:04,186 --> 00:29:05,487
You show up here

636
00:29:05,520 --> 00:29:07,022
and you're dressed
like one of them

637
00:29:07,056 --> 00:29:08,299
and now you're telling
me that you know

638
00:29:08,323 --> 00:29:10,159
what they're
planning to do? How?

639
00:29:10,192 --> 00:29:11,893
You need to trust me.

640
00:29:11,926 --> 00:29:13,095
How can I do that?

641
00:29:13,129 --> 00:29:15,430
You're a fugitive who ran.

642
00:29:15,463 --> 00:29:16,564
Because I was framed.

643
00:29:16,598 --> 00:29:19,168
Then why not let me help you?

644
00:29:19,201 --> 00:29:20,702
Because you can't.

645
00:29:20,735 --> 00:29:22,379
You asked me before if
I knew what that coin

646
00:29:22,403 --> 00:29:24,073
they found on my dad meant.

647
00:29:24,106 --> 00:29:25,707
I didn't know then.

648
00:29:25,740 --> 00:29:27,709
But I do now.

649
00:29:27,742 --> 00:29:30,179
It's the symbol of
the Court of Owls.

650
00:29:30,212 --> 00:29:32,490
They're a secret cabal that's
been pulling strings in Gotham

651
00:29:32,514 --> 00:29:34,183
since the city was founded.

652
00:29:34,216 --> 00:29:35,483
Turner, this is insane.

653
00:29:35,517 --> 00:29:38,820
Listen. The Court
killed my dad.

654
00:29:40,588 --> 00:29:41,956
And now they're
trying to kill me.

655
00:29:43,092 --> 00:29:44,325
And the others.

656
00:29:45,261 --> 00:29:46,828
We can't trust anyone.

657
00:29:48,097 --> 00:29:49,430
Then why trust me?

658
00:29:50,899 --> 00:29:52,467
Because my dad did.

659
00:29:59,108 --> 00:30:00,575
What do you need me to do?

660
00:30:04,213 --> 00:30:06,224
Harper: We could try to cut
off the outflow of the aerosol.

661
00:30:06,248 --> 00:30:07,882
Stop it from releasing the gas.

662
00:30:07,916 --> 00:30:09,560
And if the stainless steel
can't contain the pressure,

663
00:30:09,584 --> 00:30:11,029
then, congratulations,
you've just turned

664
00:30:11,053 --> 00:30:12,363
a chemical bomb
into a regular bomb.

665
00:30:12,387 --> 00:30:14,256
I suppose you have
a better idea?

666
00:30:14,290 --> 00:30:15,824
Yeah. Not doing your idea.

667
00:30:15,857 --> 00:30:17,492
Right, because Gotham
Academy is renowned

668
00:30:17,525 --> 00:30:19,228
for its Honors Bomb
Defusing classes.

669
00:30:19,261 --> 00:30:21,763
Nope, just basic science.

670
00:30:21,796 --> 00:30:23,565
We're better off
disrupting the power source

671
00:30:23,598 --> 00:30:25,500
to the valve that
pressurizes it.

672
00:30:25,533 --> 00:30:27,836
That's your solution?
Cut the wire?

673
00:30:27,869 --> 00:30:29,771
What's next? Bang
on it with a hammer?

674
00:30:29,804 --> 00:30:31,515
The Mutants could've built
in a hidden redundancy,

675
00:30:31,539 --> 00:30:33,075
in which case you
cut the primary,

676
00:30:33,108 --> 00:30:35,743
this thing hot-boxes half
the city's power players.

677
00:30:35,777 --> 00:30:37,412
Oh, uh, and us.

678
00:30:37,445 --> 00:30:39,114
[Radio chirps] Carrie:
Can you read me?

679
00:30:39,148 --> 00:30:41,317
Me and Duela took out as
many Mutants as we could.

680
00:30:41,349 --> 00:30:43,551
All that's left are the
ones in the Gallery.

681
00:30:43,585 --> 00:30:45,353
How are you two
doing down there?

682
00:30:48,190 --> 00:30:49,424
Can I talk to you?

683
00:30:49,457 --> 00:30:50,692
You have to recall the order

684
00:30:50,725 --> 00:30:52,027
to release the Mutant Leader.

685
00:30:52,061 --> 00:30:53,329
Why the hell would I do that?

686
00:30:53,361 --> 00:30:54,801
Because if you don't,
we're all dead.

687
00:30:54,829 --> 00:30:56,340
It's a double-cross.
They're gonna gas this place

688
00:30:56,364 --> 00:30:57,932
the moment you set him free.

689
00:30:57,966 --> 00:30:59,868
Who told you that?

690
00:30:59,901 --> 00:31:02,670
I'm asking you to please
just trust me on this.

691
00:31:02,704 --> 00:31:04,539
Trust the guy that wants my job?

692
00:31:10,712 --> 00:31:12,047
Man: Prisoner coming through.

693
00:31:16,218 --> 00:31:18,786
Delta on point.
Transfer team ready.

694
00:31:21,656 --> 00:31:23,092
Let's move him out now.

695
00:31:25,361 --> 00:31:26,794
[Cell phone chimes]

696
00:31:29,131 --> 00:31:30,798
And things just got worse.

697
00:31:31,900 --> 00:31:33,740
Cullen says they've
released the Mutant Leader.

698
00:31:35,603 --> 00:31:37,082
Carrie, you guys need
to take out the rest of

699
00:31:37,106 --> 00:31:38,873
those Mutants, like, now.

700
00:31:38,907 --> 00:31:41,843
As you requested,
Vernon Wagner has been

701
00:31:41,876 --> 00:31:44,246
released into the sewer system.

702
00:31:44,280 --> 00:31:45,813
Well ahead of your deadline.

703
00:31:45,847 --> 00:31:47,949
[Cell phone rings]

704
00:31:47,982 --> 00:31:49,118
That's probably him now.

705
00:31:49,151 --> 00:31:50,718
[Cell phone ringing]

706
00:31:53,521 --> 00:31:56,058
Vernon on phone: I'm
in the subway system.

707
00:31:56,091 --> 00:31:57,425
You are good to go.

708
00:32:00,495 --> 00:32:02,398
Our leader's been released!

709
00:32:02,430 --> 00:32:04,699
[Mutants cheering]

710
00:32:06,101 --> 00:32:09,604
Now you will all be free.

711
00:32:15,110 --> 00:32:17,079
Uhh!

712
00:32:17,112 --> 00:32:19,114
[Both grunting]

713
00:32:41,469 --> 00:32:42,770
Turner: Whatever
you're gonna do,

714
00:32:42,804 --> 00:32:44,440
do it now.

715
00:32:44,472 --> 00:32:46,141
Turner: We have to
shut that bomb down.

716
00:32:47,076 --> 00:32:49,144
OK, I'm gonna disable
the pressure valve.

717
00:32:49,178 --> 00:32:50,245
Too late.

718
00:32:50,279 --> 00:32:51,479
Wait, no!

719
00:33:02,824 --> 00:33:03,725
[Both grunt]

720
00:33:03,758 --> 00:33:05,593
[Thud] [Crowd cheering]

721
00:33:05,626 --> 00:33:07,329
Officer: Freeze! Police!

722
00:33:07,363 --> 00:33:09,897
[Cheering and applause]

723
00:33:25,616 --> 00:33:27,817
What the hell was that?

724
00:33:29,285 --> 00:33:30,721
Excuse me?

725
00:33:30,754 --> 00:33:32,155
You know what I'm talking about.

726
00:33:32,188 --> 00:33:34,123
You mean the part where
I saved our lives?

727
00:33:34,157 --> 00:33:36,527
No, the part where you
took a chance with my life.

728
00:33:36,560 --> 00:33:38,861
Which you still
have, thanks to me.

729
00:33:38,895 --> 00:33:40,997
You cut the wire without
knowing what would happen.

730
00:33:41,030 --> 00:33:42,932
Because I knew what
would happen if I didn't.

731
00:33:42,965 --> 00:33:44,744
You do realize the only
way you win this argument

732
00:33:44,768 --> 00:33:46,135
is by being dead, right?

733
00:33:46,169 --> 00:33:47,671
No, because my way
would have worked,

734
00:33:47,705 --> 00:33:49,181
only you didn't give
me a chance because

735
00:33:49,205 --> 00:33:50,873
I didn't go to some
fancy private school,

736
00:33:50,907 --> 00:33:52,643
but that does not make
you smarter than me.

737
00:33:52,676 --> 00:33:54,043
I never said that.

738
00:33:54,077 --> 00:33:56,547
Yeah. You did when
you cut that wire.

739
00:33:57,847 --> 00:34:00,149
This isn't your
daddy's game show.

740
00:34:00,183 --> 00:34:01,960
Now, why don't you go
back to your cozy bedroom

741
00:34:01,984 --> 00:34:03,587
on the top floor
of your mansion.

742
00:34:04,921 --> 00:34:06,523
Easier to look down
on me from there.

743
00:34:12,228 --> 00:34:14,598
Man on TV: While the hostage
situation has been resolved,

744
00:34:14,631 --> 00:34:18,101
the leader of the Mutant
Gang is once again at large,

745
00:34:18,134 --> 00:34:20,337
but Gotham can rest
a bit easier tonight,

746
00:34:20,371 --> 00:34:23,807
thanks in part to the heroic
efforts... and fists...

747
00:34:23,841 --> 00:34:26,142
Of District Attorney
Harvey Dent.

748
00:34:29,078 --> 00:34:31,914
Mr. Dent, we didn't find any
explosive devices on the premises.

749
00:34:31,948 --> 00:34:34,183
What? He had a detonator.

750
00:34:34,217 --> 00:34:37,688
We swept the facility,
including the ventilator ducts.

751
00:34:37,721 --> 00:34:40,123
Nothing. Maybe the
Mutants were bluffing

752
00:34:40,156 --> 00:34:41,425
to get their leader out.

753
00:34:42,693 --> 00:34:43,893
Damn it.

754
00:34:45,094 --> 00:34:47,263
So, we save everyone's lives

755
00:34:47,296 --> 00:34:49,433
and Harvey Dent
gets all the credit?

756
00:34:50,367 --> 00:34:52,201
Look, he can have
the credit as long as

757
00:34:52,235 --> 00:34:53,970
we can have the shiny stuff.

758
00:34:56,707 --> 00:34:58,675
And what the Mutants take...

759
00:34:58,709 --> 00:35:00,009
[Gasp]

760
00:35:00,042 --> 00:35:01,911
we taketh away.

761
00:35:04,147 --> 00:35:06,983
I know what you're gonna
say. "This is so wrong.

762
00:35:07,016 --> 00:35:09,218
The gala guests
were victims, too."

763
00:35:15,726 --> 00:35:17,126
Not all of them.

764
00:35:20,864 --> 00:35:22,098
It's a Court of Owls watch.

765
00:35:22,131 --> 00:35:23,600
Just like the one Ford had.

766
00:35:27,805 --> 00:35:29,071
So is this one.

767
00:35:31,408 --> 00:35:32,719
The Court of Owls
were at the gala

768
00:35:32,743 --> 00:35:34,010
and we didn't even know it.

769
00:35:34,043 --> 00:35:35,512
There were over
200 people there.

770
00:35:35,546 --> 00:35:37,524
Which means we have no way
of knowing who they are.

771
00:35:37,548 --> 00:35:39,850
Well, maybe this will
help us find them.

772
00:35:39,883 --> 00:35:41,385
As promised. Every
scrap of paper

773
00:35:41,418 --> 00:35:43,186
the GCPD has on
Alan Wayne's death.

774
00:35:43,219 --> 00:35:45,556
Autopsy reports, eyewitness
statements, all of it.

775
00:35:45,589 --> 00:35:47,300
If the Court did kill
him, hopefully there's

776
00:35:47,324 --> 00:35:49,225
something in here
that'll lead us to them.

777
00:35:58,769 --> 00:36:00,002
Uhh!

778
00:36:02,104 --> 00:36:04,341
Think I'll do your
sparring partner a favor

779
00:36:04,374 --> 00:36:05,676
and call a TKO.

780
00:36:08,044 --> 00:36:09,245
They let him go.

781
00:36:10,213 --> 00:36:12,783
After everything the
Mutant Leader has done,

782
00:36:12,816 --> 00:36:14,150
and all the people he's hurt.

783
00:36:15,953 --> 00:36:17,186
And they let him go.

784
00:36:18,187 --> 00:36:20,791
I know. It's insane.

785
00:36:20,824 --> 00:36:22,058
It's Gotham.

786
00:36:24,328 --> 00:36:28,665
You try to change it
and it just changes you.

787
00:36:31,735 --> 00:36:33,403
Makes me wonder
why I even do it.

788
00:36:34,371 --> 00:36:36,005
Because you're
really good at it.

789
00:36:42,346 --> 00:36:45,682
Not easy to say it,
but I gotta admit:

790
00:36:47,851 --> 00:36:49,218
I'm jealous of you.

791
00:36:51,020 --> 00:36:53,155
I see why my dad wanted
you as his Robin.

792
00:36:56,125 --> 00:36:58,929
I just wish I'd gotten
to see that side of him.

793
00:36:58,962 --> 00:37:01,999
Turner... you got to
see the side of him

794
00:37:02,031 --> 00:37:03,967
that I never did.

795
00:37:04,001 --> 00:37:07,704
The man who takes his
kid on camping trips.

796
00:37:10,841 --> 00:37:12,041
Dad.

797
00:37:15,177 --> 00:37:17,514
I was so young when my dad died.

798
00:37:21,018 --> 00:37:23,453
I never got to experience
that kind of stuff.

799
00:37:27,758 --> 00:37:30,460
So, I'm jealous of you.

800
00:37:32,161 --> 00:37:33,964
Well, it's clear
from his journals

801
00:37:33,997 --> 00:37:35,465
how much he cared about you.

802
00:37:37,401 --> 00:37:40,269
It's also clear just
how responsible he felt

803
00:37:40,304 --> 00:37:42,104
for every bad thing
that every bad guy

804
00:37:42,138 --> 00:37:44,240
did in Gotham that
he didn't stop.

805
00:37:45,742 --> 00:37:47,678
It was eating him up inside.

806
00:37:47,711 --> 00:37:49,746
And I can't imagine
he'd want that for you.

807
00:37:51,280 --> 00:37:53,617
My dad didn't want me
going down his path.

808
00:37:54,818 --> 00:37:56,553
And I may never know why.

809
00:37:58,455 --> 00:38:02,258
But I do know...
following in his footsteps

810
00:38:02,291 --> 00:38:04,494
makes me feel closer to him.

811
00:38:05,862 --> 00:38:08,398
He wouldn't want you to bear
the weight of his legacy alone.

812
00:38:09,900 --> 00:38:11,233
Let me help you.

813
00:38:14,438 --> 00:38:16,840
Risking your freedom to
save all those people?

814
00:38:18,041 --> 00:38:20,444
It was very brave.
And, Turner,

815
00:38:20,477 --> 00:38:22,679
your dad would be
so proud of you.

816
00:38:24,047 --> 00:38:26,215
Is that a yes? Come on.

817
00:38:26,248 --> 00:38:29,319
What did you say that
night you followed my dad?

818
00:38:29,353 --> 00:38:31,355
What convinced him
to let you help him?

819
00:38:31,388 --> 00:38:33,824
I didn't convince
him. Not that time.

820
00:38:34,958 --> 00:38:37,060
He said no. And then
I followed him again

821
00:38:37,094 --> 00:38:39,195
and then I asked him
again and he said no.

822
00:38:39,228 --> 00:38:40,797
Actually, I got a lot of nos.

823
00:38:42,332 --> 00:38:43,734
But I just kept on asking.

824
00:38:47,337 --> 00:38:48,705
I guess I never gave up.

825
00:38:50,507 --> 00:38:53,175
Kinda sucks to be the
Mutant Leader then.

826
00:38:53,209 --> 00:38:54,745
With that kind of persistence...

827
00:38:56,680 --> 00:38:58,180
he won't be free for long.

828
00:39:15,365 --> 00:39:17,734
Was not easy, but I got it.

829
00:39:17,768 --> 00:39:20,337
Not sure why you wanted
that from evidence lockup.

830
00:39:20,370 --> 00:39:21,838
I thought you hated him.

831
00:39:21,872 --> 00:39:23,674
Oh, I do.

832
00:39:23,707 --> 00:39:25,876
This is just so I
don't forget how much.

833
00:39:30,981 --> 00:39:32,281
Harper: Cullen?

834
00:39:32,315 --> 00:39:33,817
No, I don't want to hear it.

835
00:39:33,850 --> 00:39:35,752
You walked into a building
with a bomb in it.

836
00:39:35,786 --> 00:39:37,530
You're the last person
who gets to lecture me

837
00:39:37,554 --> 00:39:39,532
about doing something
dangerous. I can handle myself.

838
00:39:39,556 --> 00:39:41,758
Harper: I know that.
Cullen: Really?

839
00:39:41,792 --> 00:39:43,803
'Cause you've been treating me
like some weak, scared, little kid.

840
00:39:43,827 --> 00:39:46,096
Harper: Cullen. Winona
Oak: ♪ This love from me ♪

841
00:39:46,129 --> 00:39:47,440
♪ I don't... ♪
Harper: You've never

842
00:39:47,464 --> 00:39:48,865
backed down from a fight.

843
00:39:50,000 --> 00:39:54,203
Not against Dad,
not against anybody.

844
00:39:55,172 --> 00:39:59,275
Cullen, you are the
bravest person I know.

845
00:39:59,309 --> 00:40:03,245
Winona Oak: ♪ I'll
be fine, I promise ♪

846
00:40:03,279 --> 00:40:05,515
I learned that from my
pain-in-the-ass sister, so.

847
00:40:05,549 --> 00:40:09,319
Winona Oak: ♪ It's
all too late ♪

848
00:40:09,352 --> 00:40:13,790
♪ So I'll stay till I break ♪

849
00:40:14,725 --> 00:40:17,060
I've been a citizen of
Gotham my whole life.

850
00:40:17,094 --> 00:40:21,064
I grew up in Cobble Hill, just
across the river. [Crowd cheering]

851
00:40:21,098 --> 00:40:22,933
Ha ha! That's right.

852
00:40:25,569 --> 00:40:31,575
For as long as I can remember,
unchecked crime and corruption

853
00:40:31,608 --> 00:40:35,746
have cast a dark
shadow over this city.

854
00:40:35,779 --> 00:40:39,483
And I think it's time we
remind those criminals

855
00:40:39,516 --> 00:40:42,486
that we are not helpless.

856
00:40:42,519 --> 00:40:47,224
We will no longer live
in the grip of fear.

857
00:40:47,256 --> 00:40:50,160
That we will fight
for a better Gotham,

858
00:40:50,193 --> 00:40:54,564
[Crowd cheering] fight
for a brighter tomorrow.

859
00:40:59,268 --> 00:41:01,404
[Buzz] Get us the
hell out of here!

860
00:41:04,508 --> 00:41:08,578
And we will let a new
dawn of hope shine down

861
00:41:08,612 --> 00:41:11,448
on the streets of
this great city.

862
00:41:11,481 --> 00:41:13,183
That is what I want.

863
00:41:13,216 --> 00:41:16,052
No! No!

864
00:41:16,086 --> 00:41:19,790
No! Oh, no! No!

865
00:41:19,823 --> 00:41:21,358
[Gasping, coughing]

866
00:41:21,391 --> 00:41:25,095
Harvey: And that
is why I am running

867
00:41:25,128 --> 00:41:27,330
for mayor of Gotham.

868
00:41:55,425 --> 00:41:57,327
Man: Greg, move your head.
